---
date: 2026-05-07T00:00:00-04:00
---

The Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus is the building that runs [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]]'s share of the [[Org/Prime Meridian/index|Prime Meridian]] rail system. It stands one story tall with a basement, behind a gate with guarded booths, and like its copies elsewhere along the horizon it is not open to the public.

Its elevators do not climb. Each one slips a single direction, starward or voidward, to the identical building fifty worlds the same way; the Org has taken a skyscraper apart into one-story floors and spread them across the horizon. [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] knows the building on sight.

Beyond the public lobby the building is a warren of catwalk flooring a foot above the ground and walls, floor and ceiling packed with cable coverings, pipes and tubes that hum and pulse with moving fluid, built to be hard for an intruder to read. [[People/Hogan Voss Darkmoor|Archmechanic Darkmoor]] keeps an office on the second floor, plain but for a pen, an inkwell and a small plaque, and can be reached by fax through the fence at the bar or by radio on a set frequency. The workers of the Submechanitor pass in silence, their heads turning together, each with rods of dull metal set into arm and throat, and the Archmechanic can drive their bodies to fight. Visitors are kept out of the rest of the building and seen out through the back exit; Low-Mechanitor Exitum-ρ-15 is one of those who walks them out.

From the lobby a freight elevator descends for what feels like five minutes into the fane of [[Org/Prime Meridian/Rapid Connection|Rapid Connection]], a ring of stone over thousands of gears of the same dull metal that runs in the staff. The elevator and the fane had gone unused for decades. Keystone 14 came out of the fane.

[[Org/Concordia/index|Concordia]] has come here for the keystone. Its agents [[Org/Concordia/People/Crawford Reeves|Crawford Reeves]] and [[Org/Concordia/People/Louis Maller|Louis Maller]] died in the lobby, with the six Happy Time Enforcers they brought. A blue light flashed from the enforcers' eyes as they died, the same blue that shines along the skin and veins of the constructs that work for [[Org/Belvedere/index|Belvedere]]; [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] takes it as a sign that the enforcers carry some mechanical augmentation, though no body has been examined. The agents carried no identification.
